Falsifies `extensible_host_controller_interface::verification::a_device_context_index_is_one_to_thirty_one_and_distinct`.

The defect: the device context index drops the direction bit, so an endpoint's IN and OUT directions share one index and one context.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_ne!` of the indexes of two different endpoints, on addresses that differ only in the direction bit.

diff --git a/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/context.rs b/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/context.rs
index a7cd23fee..90764d7d6 100644
--- a/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/context.rs
+++ b/crates/extensible_host_controller_interface/src/context.rs
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ pub const fn endpoint_index(address: u8) -> u8 {
     if number == 0 {
         1
     } else {
-        number * 2 + (address >> 7)
+        number * 2
     }
 }
 
